stagerig-os (0.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Background services and timers that wake up by themselves are switched
    off: systemd-oomd, crash reporting, cups-browsed, ModemManager, and the
    timers for firmware lists, the manual index, apt, Ubuntu Pro and the
    disk trim. Removing the package switches the same ones back on.
  * stagerig-os-update trims the disk and refreshes the firmware list.
  * Wifi power saving is off.
  * stagerig-os-check has a Background services section, and mentions
    wifi and Bluetooth when they are on.

 -- Donnie Guedry <dguedry@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:15:00 -0600

stagerig-os (0.3.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * The dock holds StageRig, VST Environment, the browser and the file
    manager, in place of Ubuntu's mail, music, office, App Center and Help.
  * Drives are no longer shown in the dock; they are in the file manager.

 -- Donnie Guedry <dguedry@gmail.com>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:30:00 -0600

stagerig-os (0.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * The wallpaper comes in six screen shapes (16:9, 16:10, 3:2, 4:3, 21:9
    and 32:9) and the one nearest the main screen is chosen at login and
    whenever a screen is connected, so the wordmark sits in the corner on
    every screen. On 16:9 it is back where it was drawn.

